From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SR_team <me@sr.team>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:55:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] nak: handle the last active subgroup invocation

nir_opt_uniform_atomics emits last_invocation when an atomic has a
subgroup-uniform address, a divergent increment and a used return value.
The combined scan/reduction path needs the last active lane, but NAK
rejected that intrinsic and returned VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN from pipeline
creation. Baldur's Gate 3 reaches this path through D3D11/DXVK.

Lower it to ballot(true) followed by an unsigned find-most-significant-bit.
The ballot reflects the executing lanes, so sparse masks and divergent
control flow select the last active lane rather than assuming lane 31.
Keep uniform-atomic optimization enabled.

diff --git a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/from_nir.rs b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/from_nir.rs
index b85aa5dc739..69bb280d164 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/from_nir.rs
+++ b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/from_nir.rs
@@ -2640,6 +2640,26 @@ impl<'a> ShaderFromNir<'a> {
 
                 self.set_dst(&intrin.def, dst.into());
             }
+            nir_intrinsic_last_invocation => {
+                // NVIDIA subgroups have 32 lanes. The highest set bit of
+                // ballot(true) is the last currently active invocation,
+                // including when control flow leaves holes in the mask.
+                let active = b.alloc_ssa(RegFile::GPR);
+                b.push_op(OpVote {
+                    op: VoteOp::Any,
+                    ballot: active.into(),
+                    vote: Dst::None,
+                    pred: true.into(),
+                });
+                let dst = b.alloc_ssa(RegFile::GPR);
+                b.push_op(OpFlo {
+                    dst: dst.into(),
+                    src: active.into(),
+                    signed: false,
+                    return_shift_amount: false,
+                });
+                self.set_dst(&intrin.def, dst.into());
+            }
             nir_intrinsic_ballot => {
                 assert!(srcs[0].bit_size() == 1);
                 let src = self.get_src(&srcs[0]);
-- 
